{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"09d27a55e23f0042ba096ed63e33a748cb4e944e664ac5e7d437375198cfe694","digest":{"component_or_area":"doctor command / mapping diagnostics","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","mapping_config.load_mapping_config","MappingConfigError","mapping_probe.build_probe","config.projects","effective_status_map","effective_type_map","effective_link_map","assert_type_decisions_complete","capability_installed","jira_datacenter","JIRA_PAT","resolve_jira_datacenter_settings","docs/user-guide.md"],"problem_keywords":["mapping config diagnostics","offline checks","live drift detection","portability","jira datacenter optional","degradation handling"],"propositions":["Offline mapping-config checks must detect and report load-time errors (non-integer hierarchy, malformed blocks) and resolve-time errors (out-of-vocabulary, unmapped-non-skipped values) as error findings with non-zero exit, without importing jira adapters","Live-drift checks against Jira vocabulary (status, type, link) must run only when jira-datacenter extra is installed and credentials resolve, with each configured-vs-observed divergence reported as a separate drift finding","Doctor must degrade gracefully when jira-datacenter extra is absent, credentials are empty, settings resolution fails, or probe transport times out, emitting a single unavailable finding and returning success","All-empty projects config stubs must be reported as warning findings (not errors) without blocking successful exit","Hierarchy divergence is excluded from live-drift checks because Data Center probe never observes hierarchyLevel, though offline hierarchy validation remains covered","Mapping diagnostics findings must be kept in a separate list from scan-dirty/lock reports and not passed to run_repair iteration, preserving the blocking-edge contract"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787903568114152001,"uuid":"b67f8dbd-a40f-4b4d-b444-7f8a99b02152"}